hls: an initialization section read that fails part way is no section

update_init_section() took what read_from_url() returned for the whole
section. avio_read() returns the bytes it read when a later read of the
section fails, and the error stays in the input's context: an interrupt
(AVERROR_EXIT), or a connection closed before the section's end, which
http reports as EIO for a body of known length (hls opens every request
with seekable=1, so http.c's premature-end check applies, no reconnect
options needed). A cut section was stored as complete: a truncated moov
went to the subdemuxer, which failed to open, and the playlist was lost
rather than one segment.

Take the input's error before it is closed and return it when the read
ended in one: the section is not stored, AVERROR_EXIT is returned as it
is and the section is asked for again on the next call, another error
fails its segment as a failed request for the section does (0101). The
end of the section (EOF) is no error.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -1884,7 +1884,7 @@ static int update_init_section(struct playlist *pls, struct segment *seg)
     HLSContext *c = pls->parent->priv_data;
     int64_t sec_size;
     int64_t urlsize;
-    int ret;
+    int ret, err;
 
     if (seg->init_section == pls->cur_init_section)
         return 0;
@@ -1919,10 +1919,15 @@ static int update_init_section(struct playlist *pls, struct segment *seg)
 
     ret = read_from_url(pls, seg->init_section, pls->init_sec_buf,
                         pls->init_sec_buf_size);
+    /* a read that ended in an error (not the section's end) is no section */
+    err = pls->input->error;
     ff_format_io_close(pls->parent, &pls->input);
 
     if (ret < 0)
         return ret;
+    /* AVERROR_EXIT: the section is asked for again on the next call (0101) */
+    if (err < 0)
+        return err;
 
     pls->cur_init_section = seg->init_section;
     pls->init_sec_data_len = ret;
